cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "tensor-membrane: a holographic tensor network as a membrane — bulk logical qubits encoded across boundary physical qubits, with a real erasure decoder and a hard overlap-recall test (synthetic)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/tensor-membrane"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-11"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Synthetic, stdlib + NumPy toy: a holographic tensor network (7 boundary
  physical qubits, 3 tensor layers of 6/7/6, 2 bulk logical qubits) built
  as a working membrane. Measured: the encoding is an isometry, no single
  boundary qubit carries the bulk, the erasure threshold is 2 (worst case),
  a real least-squares decoder recovers the bulk with a noise-dependent
  threshold, and the overlap-recall gate fails honestly on non-orthogonal
  patterns (no threshold separates real from code-random; no collision
  detection). It is not a real quantum error-correcting code and not a
  real holographic duality. The repository documents measured behaviour
  and limits, including negative results.
keywords:
  - "synthetic"
  - "toy-model"
  - "tensor-network"
  - "holographic"
  - "quantum-error-correction"
  - "reproducible"
  - "python"
